  distance stats -> measurements 1, errors 0 ... ; calibration +3.7 cm, filter off, alarm on

Result: OTA-10 fully satisfied for this transition. No data-loss bug found on 2.1.0 -> 2.3.0
(unlike BUG-006, which is about 'passwd' after a plain reboot without OTA, not about OTA persistence
of the originally registered password - that part works correctly, as shown above).

Side observation (not a bug, a 2.3.0 feature note): the single 'distance 1' measurement above
automatically generated two CIC alerts ([CIC #1 WARNING] and [CIC #2 INFO]) without any 'alert'/'cic'
command being used - Alert center (AL-1) is wired into the sonar subsystem from the first measurement.

=== OTA-7 self-check: final state ===
The live 'PENDING_VERIFY ... self-check passed, firmware marked VALID' console lines from the actual
post-OTA boot were lost to the same console-encoding crash described below (the text was captured by
the driver in memory but never written to a file before the crash). What IS confirmed independently:

  version -> partition: ota_1 @ 0x1a0000, state: valid
  ota     -> running: v2.3.0 in ota_1 (valid); previous: v2.1.0 in ota_0

'state: valid' can only be reached after the self-check passes (PRD OTA-7: a freshly OTA'd partition
starts PENDING_VERIFY and only becomes VALID once the app calls the IDF 'mark valid' API after its own
checks). The device also did not roll back, which it would have done automatically had the self-check
failed. Self-check pass is therefore confirmed by this partition state, even though the live transcript
of the check itself is missing from this evidence file. A clean live capture of the same
'PENDING_VERIFY -> self-check passed' sequence (console encoding issue fixed) is in
logs/ota/ota_downgrade_and_back.log, taken during the downgrade/upgrade round done for TC-OTA-09/10/27/28.

=== Note on tooling ===
The automation script (framework/tools/ota_210_to_230.py) crashed printing the post-reboot boot log to
the Windows console (cp1251 code page cannot encode the '°C' character in a temperature-sensor line).
The OTA itself had already completed and the device had already rebooted into 2.3.0 before the crash;
the AFTER snapshot above was captured in a follow-up connection (hence the second 'last reset: power on'
boot log - that second reset is an RTS hardware reset issued by the verification script, not the OTA
reboot in the previous section, whose own 'success: v2.1.0 -> v2.3.0' / 'Rebooting...' and self-check are
visible in the raw run output). Fixed for future runs: script now writes UTF-8 regardless of console
code page.
